#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Element of the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4055c931-9c69-5293-9813-b782ee0735a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279516} {:answer/id #uuid "4b5ebfe8-4222-5d74-911a-9ab1f9988bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279517} {:answer/id #uuid "72785da6-d489-5693-8457-2c0ca9a138bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{44}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279518} {:answer/id #uuid "dd74a7fb-9fb1-5ae8-908b-5e9a223aa2ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{44}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279519} {:answer/id #uuid "04ee1b6b-8b93-5f8c-ba7d-55eb490d6b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4055c931-9c69-5293-9813-b782ee0735a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279516} :answer-field/id #uuid "27ebd8d4-01ee-506c-b9cf-53cda8dd55f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279515}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5434732d-193f-528d-b9d5-29d58f90d985" :question/math-academy-id "q-18281" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-4|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(0+9)-4(0-6)+1(0+2) \\\\  & =18+24+2 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0-6) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}=\\frac{1}{44}\\cdot 6=\\frac{3}{22}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
